# Citation metadata. ORCIDs, funding and the release date are added when available.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "cowmrp: Markov reward process models of dairy cattle"
abstract: >-
  A Python package of Markov reward process (MRP) models of dairy cattle: a domain-free MRP engine with a cow domain
  (state: lactation, days in milk, days pregnant) and a youngstock domain. It values cows (keep or replace), projects a herd
  forward with the expected distribution, stochastic paths or Monte Carlo, and reports environmental outputs beside economic ones.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24357536
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bovi-analytics/cow-mrp"
url: "https://bovi-analytics.github.io/cow-mrp/"
keywords:
  - markov reward process
  - dairy cattle
  - replacement
  - simulation
  - livestock
